hexagon: write the final GATED_DELTA_NET state through the cache when it shares a line
Fold-into: upstream/hexagon-host

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The output of GATED_DELTA_NET holds the attention output, then the final state
(snapshot slot 0), then the other snapshot slots. The kernel writes the
attention output and the slots 1 and up with stores through the L2 cache, and
the final state with a DMA write to DDR. When the size of the attention output
(S_v * H * tokens * sequences * 4 bytes) is not a multiple of the 128-byte L2
line, the last line of the attention output also holds the first bytes of the
final state. That line is dirty in L2 with the old bytes of the state, and its
write-back replaces the bytes of the DMA write.

This patch writes the final state through the cache when its first byte is not
on a line boundary. Each state is S_v * S_v floats, a multiple of the line,
thus all states of the op then take the same path. With S_v = 128 the
attention output ends on a line boundary, thus those shapes keep the DMA path.

